From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 18:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: remove unused platform device

EDMA IRQ discovery uses the ethernet device's child node and
of_irq_get_byname().  The old platform-device conversion is no longer
used and fails W=1 builds with an unused-but-set-variable error.

Remove the dead variable and assignment without changing IRQ lookup.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-ppe/-/tree/87bb9b326dfe7ddafb2cc8bc588e74d552a2a9b5
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma.c
@@ -513,11 +513,9 @@ static int edma_irq_configure(void)
 	struct edma_ring_info *rx = hw_info->rx;
 	char edma_irq_name[EDMA_IRQ_NAME_SIZE];
 	struct device *dev = ppe_dev->dev;
-	struct platform_device *pdev;
 	struct device_node *edma_np;
 	u32 i;
 
-	pdev = to_platform_device(dev);
 	edma_np = of_get_child_by_name(dev->of_node, EDMA_NODE_NAME);
 	edma_ctx->intr_info.intr_txcmpl = kzalloc((sizeof(*edma_ctx->intr_info.intr_txcmpl) *
 						  txcmpl->num_rings), GFP_KERNEL);
-- 
2.43.0
